Microsoft Learn: Manage Identities and Governance in Microsoft Entra ID

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Manage Identities and Governance in Microsoft Entra ID
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to create, configure, and manage identities in Microsoft Entra ID to secure access to cloud resources and implement centralized identity governance.

This module focused on user and group management, license administration, device registration, security attributes, and automatic provisioning to support secure access control in Azure environments.

Step 1: Understanding Microsoft Entra ID

The module introduced Microsoft Entra ID as Microsoft's cloud-based identity and access management service.

Microsoft Entra ID provides centralized identity management for:

Employees
Administrators
Contractors
Vendors
Applications
Devices

Key benefits:

Single Sign-On (SSO)
Multifactor Authentication (MFA)
Centralized identity management
Secure resource access
Identity governance
Integration with Azure services

The module emphasized that identity management is a critical component of cloud security and Zero Trust architecture.

Step 2: Creating, Configuring, and Managing Users

The training covered how user accounts are managed within Microsoft Entra ID.

User types studied:

User Type	Description
Cloud Identities	Users managed directly in Microsoft Entra ID
Directory-Synchronized Identities	Users synchronized from on-premises Active Directory
Guest Users	External users invited into the organization

Skills practiced:

Creating user accounts
Updating user properties
Resetting passwords
Managing user access
Assigning administrative roles
Removing users

Key concepts learned:

Authentication verifies user identity
Authorization determines resource permissions
Guest users provide secure external collaboration
Directory synchronization supports hybrid environments

The module emphasized controlling access through proper identity management practices.

Step 3: Creating, Configuring, and Managing Groups

The module introduced groups as a way to simplify permission management.

Group types explored:

Group Type	Purpose
Security Groups	Control access to resources
Microsoft 365 Groups	Support collaboration and productivity services

Benefits of groups:

Simplified permission assignment
Centralized access management
Reduced administrative overhead
Improved scalability

Key lessons learned:

Permissions should be assigned to groups rather than individual users whenever possible
Groups support role-based access management
Group membership can simplify large-scale administration

The module highlighted groups as a best practice for managing organizational access.

